<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span><span id="S4.T2.22" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ModernBERT-Chat evaluation results.</span> ModernBERT-Chat <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Warner et al., 2025</a>)</cite> and GPT-2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Radford et al., 2019</a>)</cite> models are evaluated with <span id="S4.T2.23" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">dLLM</span>’s pipeline; Qwen1.5 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bai et al., 2023</a>)</cite> numbers are reported by original sources. See Figure <a href="#A1.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ Appendix A Training Curves ‣ dLLM: Simple Diffusion Language Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> for training curves.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S4.T3" class="ltx_table">
<table id="S4.T3.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
